<div style="color:#111111;" class="rounded p-6 gap-3 bg-light text-dark" data-zesty-id="content:wysiwyg_basic:2:53"><p>
	 
</p>

<p>
	For over 30 years, The Salvation Army Hampton Roads Area Command, with the help of our community partners and donors, has worked to ensure that children in Hampton Roads start the new school year with the “Write Stuff." The Write Stuff back-to-school initiative is an annual event that distributes backpacks filled with school supplies to students in grades K through 12 who reside in Norfolk, Chesapeake, Virginia Beach, Portsmouth, Suffolk, and Western Tidewater.
</p>

<p>
	<span style="color:#212121;"><span style="tab-stops:list .5in;"></span></span>
</p></div>
<div class="py-5" data-zesty-id="design:design:whitespace-xl:3:85"></div>
<div class="py-5" data-zesty-id="design:design:whitespace-xl:4:44"></div>
<div style="color:#111111;" class="rounded p-6 gap-3 bg-light text-dark" data-zesty-id="content:wysiwyg_basic:5:71"><p style="text-align:center;">
	<strong>2026 WRITE Stuff distribution information</strong>
</p>

<p style="text-align:center;">
	The Salvation Army is helping local K–12 students get ready for the new school year with our Write Stuff Backpack Distribution. We’ll Be providing free backpacks filled with school supplies to students in need — while supplies last!
</p>

<p style="text-align:center;">
	 <u><strong>Distribution Locations &amp; Dates</strong></u>
</p>

<p style="text-align:center;">
	<u>Kroc Center Hampton Roads</u>
</p>

<p style="text-align:center;">
	1401 Ballentine Blvd, Norfolk, VA
</p>

<p style="text-align:center;">
	August 14, 2026 | 4:00 pm to 7:00 pm
</p>

<p style="text-align:center;">
	August 15, 2026 | 9:00 am to 12 Noon
</p>

<p style="text-align:center;">
	Our Kroc Center distribution is open to residents of Norfolk, Chesapeake, and Virginia Beach
</p>

<p style="text-align:center;">
	<u>Portsmouth Corps</u>
</p>

<p style="text-align:center;">
	2306 Airline Blvd, Portsmouth, VA
</p>

<p style="text-align:center;">
	August 14, 2026 | 4:00 pm to 7:00 pm
</p>

<p style="text-align:center;">
	Our Portsmouth Corps distribution is open to residents of Portsmouth (any zip code) and Chesapeake residents living in zip codes 23321 and 23323 only
</p>

<p style="text-align:center;">
	<u>Suffolk Corps</u>
</p>

<p style="text-align:center;">
	400 Bank St, Suffolk, VA
</p>

<p style="text-align:center;">
	August 8, 2026 | 10:00 am to 12 Noon
</p>

<p style="text-align:center;">
	Our Suffolk Corps distribution is open to residents of Suffolk and Western Tidewater
</p>

<p style="text-align:center;">
	<u><strong>Required Documentation</strong></u>
</p>

<p style="text-align:center;">
	Valid government-issued photo ID for parent or guardian (not expired)
</p>

<p style="text-align:center;">
	Proof of residency
</p>

<p style="text-align:center;">
	Child’s Birth certificate
</p>

<p style="text-align:center;">
	For more information, please call the Hampton Roads Area Command at <a href="tel:7575438100">757-543-8100</a> or scan the qr code on the flyer.
</p>

<p>
	 
</p>

<p style="text-align:center;" class="cta-button-group d-flex flex-wrap gap-2 my-3 justify-content-center"><a href="https://s3.amazonaws.com/uss-cache.salvationarmy.org/9567790c-1545-4bbd-80ed-c296e91cf19a_26+WS+Client+Flyer_All.pdf" class="btn btn-secondary gap-1 mt-2">Download Flyer Here</a></p>

<p style="text-align:center;">
	<strong><em>You can support this important fundraiser by becoming a sponsor, making a donation, or dropping off school supplies. To donate supplies or participate in a supply donation drive, please contact: <br>
